<article class="story-copy">
  <p class="lead">Before students headed back to class, KCMC surrounded them with prayer, encouragement and a simple reminder they can carry with them every day: they are loved, they are not alone, and God goes with them wherever they go.</p>

  <h2>What happened</h2>
  <p>Students came forward with their backpacks while church leaders and volunteers prayed over them. The blessing focused on the ordinary places where faith becomes real during a school day — working with their hands, learning with their minds, making friends with their hearts, finding courage when they are afraid, and remembering they are loved.</p>

  <div class="impact-grid" aria-label="Backpack Blessing highlights">
    <section class="impact-card"><strong>Students were seen and prayed for.</strong><p>The moment centered the children and youth themselves, not a program or promotion.</p></section>
    <section class="impact-card"><strong>Families were included.</strong><p>The prayer extends beyond the classroom to parents, caregivers, teachers and everyone walking beside these students.</p></section>
    <section class="impact-card"><strong>Faith became practical.</strong><p>The blessing gives students language they can remember when school feels exciting, difficult, lonely or uncertain.</p></section>
    <section class="impact-card"><strong>The church showed up together.</strong><p>This is KCMC in action: congregation, leaders and children sharing one moment of encouragement and community.</p></section>
  </div>

  <div class="story-quote">“When I am brave, be my strength. When I am afraid, be my courage. And wherever I go, help me remember: I am loved. Always.”</div>

  <div class="blessing-grid">
    <section class="blessing-card">
      <h2>A Blessing for Your Backpack</h2>
      <p>God, walk with me today.<br>Bless my hands as I work,<br>my mind as I learn,<br>and my heart as I make friends.<br>When I am brave, be my strength.<br>When I am afraid, be my courage.<br>And wherever I go, help me remember:</p>
      <p class="emphasis">I am loved. Always.</p>
      <p>Amen.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="blessing-card">
      <h2>Be Strong and Courageous</h2>
      <p class="emphasis">“Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged, for the Lord your God will be with you wherever you go.”</p>
      <p><strong>Joshua 1:9</strong></p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <h2>Why this belongs in KCMC Connect</h2>
  <p>KCMC Connect should not only tell people what the church offers. It should show what the church is actually doing. Stories like this give members, visitors and families a living record of ministry happening in the congregation and community.</p>

